# `q.toLowerCase()` on a text that no turn changes ran in every turn. It runs no code of the program and cannot fail but for lack of memory; the receiver is proven a text in front of the typed copy (it was written one: the
# test stands in front, and its no leads to the closed copy). It is called once, behind the yes of the head's own question: a loop of no turn pays nothing.
# The closed copy is printed first, with its own call. The block in front of the typed copy is printed behind its head: the call, its box, and the jump to the head.
# RUN: walk f1:Body mechanisms=all
# CHECK: ) isInLoop=true isLoopHead=true:
# CHECK: inlineBuiltin=StringToLowerCase
# CHECK-NEXT: = Box
# CHECK-NEXT: Jump -> next
# CHECK-NOT: inlineBuiltin=StringToLowerCase
